[
    {
        "content": "<p>Why isn't <code>[ , ]</code> and <code>( , )</code> a user extensible notation the way <code>· + · </code> and other operations are?</p>\n<p>I have a custom type and I would really like to have <code>( , )</code> notation for it. I tried writing coersions from/to product types but pattern matching <code>let (a,b) := x</code> does not work this way.</p>\n<p>Maybe we could also stop inventing new  notations <code>#[ , ]</code>, <code>#v[ , ]</code>, <code>![ , ]</code>, <code>!₂[ , ]</code>, <code>!![ , ]</code>, ...</p>",
        "id": 603629945,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1781594967
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, for example, Swift has a version of this with the <a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/ExpressibleByArrayLiteral\"><code>ExpressibleByArrayLiteral</code></a> protocol (type class).</p>",
        "id": 603682699,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcus Rossel",
        "timestamp": 1781605263
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I did thumbs up this proposal, since it could be nice to be able to extend this notation. <br>\nHowever, I've definitely used that fact that <code>(x, y)</code> has type <code>Prod a b</code> without having to specify the type explicitly, and we would lose that.</p>",
        "id": 603693748,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1781607528
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think <code>(x, y)</code> should be <code>Prod</code> if not required otherwise. The same way <code>0</code> is <code>Nat</code> by default.</p>",
        "id": 603694383,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1781607655
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, I just learned that even dot notation works for <code>Nat</code> without any type ascriptions.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- info: Nat.succ 0 : Nat -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">succ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Then this can probably be implemented with relatively limited downstream consequences.</p>",
        "id": 603696146,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1781608020
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm thinking of something like this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HListNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">expandNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>i.e. for a class of types you can provide  function of type <code>expandNotation : HList Term → MacroM (Option Term)</code> that will expand notation <code>[[2,3],4,[5,19,10]]</code> to whatever. It can return <code>none</code> if invalid.</p>",
        "id": 603862699,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1781631389
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is a prototype that can do</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">[[[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">]]]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which is accomplished by adding these two inductive instances</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HListNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">expandNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unless</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">xs'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">xs'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]))</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HListNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">HListNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HListNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">expandNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unless</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expandNotation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">xs'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xi</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">xs'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Right now, it does not default to product type if the expected type <code>ty</code> is a metavariable. </p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>code</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Qq</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</sp